<!--
    A lit diya: a lamp with a flame over it.

    ## What it replaces

    A white outline of a gift box inside a purple circle, committed in M0 under the comment
    *"Placeholder mark. A real icon is a launch task, not a walking-skeleton task."* Nine
    milestones later nothing had launched, and the icon was still Material's `#FF6750A4`.

    ## Why a diya

    This is an India-first product and the icon is the one piece of it somebody sees without
    opening the app. A diya is read instantly across the country, is not tied to one festival or
    one faith, and — the part that decided it — **it is the one warm mark that works on both
    halves of this app.** A lamp is lit for a birthday and it is lit in remembrance. A gift box,
    a cake or a balloon is only ever the first of those, and the whole visual direction was
    chosen because this app's list holds a death anniversary next to a fifth birthday.

    ## Drawing notes

    The viewport is the adaptive-icon standard 108x108. A launcher may mask anything outside the
    central 72x72 and WILL mask outside 66x66 on a circular mask, so the art sits inside
    x: 28..80, y: 29..81 — comfortably within the safe zone, which is why it survives a squircle,
    a circle and a teardrop without losing the flame's tip.

    Two colours, both from `values/colors.xml`, never literals: the flame in the accent and the
    bowl in ink, so the mark reads as an object rather than as a silhouette. The silhouette
    version — which is what Android 13+ themed icons need — is `ic_launcher_monochrome.xml`.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The flame. A teardrop with its point up, slightly narrower than it is tall. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/wk_accent"
        android:pathData="M54,29 C54,29 43,42 43,50.5 C43,57.2 47.9,62 54,62 C60.1,62 65,57.2 65,50.5 C65,42 54,29 54,29 Z" />

    <!-- The bowl. Flat lip, shallow curve — a diya, not a cup. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/wk_ink"
        android:pathData="M28,64 L80,64 C80,74 68.4,81 54,81 C39.6,81 28,74 28,64 Z" />
</vector>
